= Identity drift (artificial intelligence) — Simple =

'''Identity drift''' is when a persistent AI agent gradually moves away from identity-related goals, rules, roles, or self-information that it was meant to preserve.

This can happen through many small changes:

* old rules disappear from summaries;
* new instructions slowly replace earlier commitments;
* bad memories are reused;
* the agent's self-description changes;
* a new model or checkpoint is loaded without preserving the right state.

Identity drift is not the same as normal learning. Learning can be intentional and correct. Drift means the change was not intended or was not properly tracked.

Goal drift and persona drift are related, but narrower ideas.

